Scenario: Create draft article
	Testing the ability to create an article with Review Status Draft and check that it is not displayed on Knowledge Capture App

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Frontend Org Name 1 |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | T4                  |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             |
	| External ID      | 12341234            |
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "12341234" with the following tags
	| liferay_dxp |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Enduser1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb                 |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                       |
	| Role             | End-user                            |
	| Access           | Organization                        |
	| Email            | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                   |
	| Organization     | Frontend Org Name 1                 |
	| Language         | English                             |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)          |
	| External ID      | Enduser1                            |
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_4                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| Tags                     | knowledge_capture_flagged_article                |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | 12341234                                         |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be assigned to the group "Self Service"
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create an article with the following values
	| Ticket ID     | ${staticRequestIdList}            |
	| Template      | Fast Track Article                |
	| Name          | A simple Fast article             |
	| Description   | A simple Fast article description |
	| Review Status | Draft                             |
	And I go to the articles list and I check that the article with the name "A simple Fast article" has the review status "Draft"
	And I log into zendesk as "zendesk.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}"
	And I click on the apps button
	Then I should not be able to view an article with the name "A simple Fast article"

Scenario: Edit and view article
	Testing the ability to create and edit an article on Knowledge Capture App

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Frontend Org Name 1 |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | T4                  |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             |
	| External ID      | 12341234            |
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "12341234" with the following tags
	| liferay_dxp |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Enduser1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb                 |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                       |
	| Role             | End-user                            |
	| Access           | Organization                        |
	| Email            | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                   |
	| Organization     | Frontend Org Name 1                 |
	| Language         | English                             |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)          |
	| External ID      | Enduser1                            |
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_4                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| Tags                     | knowledge_capture_flagged_article                |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | 12341234                                         |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be assigned to the group "Self Service"
	And I log into zendesk as "zendesk.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create an article with the following values
	| Ticket ID     | ${staticRequestIdList}            |
	| Template      | DXPC Fast Track Article           |
	| Name          | A simple DXPC article             |
	| Description   | A simple DXPC article description |
	| Review Status | Published                         |
	And I log into zendesk as "zendesk.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}"
	And I click on the apps button
	Then I should be able to view an article with the name "A simple DXPC article" and description "A simple DXPC article description"
	When I edit an article with the following values
	| Article Name               | A simple DXPC article           |
	| Article Name Update        | A different article             |
	| Article Description Update | A different article description |
	| Review Status              | Published                       |
	| Review Status Update       | Published                       |
	And I log into zendesk as "zendesk.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}"
	And I click on the apps button
	Then I should be able to view an article with the name "A different article" and description "A different article description"
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}"
	And I click on the apps button
	Then I should not be able to view an article with the name "A simple DXPC article" via the article list